&lt;p&gt;SumUp is already live in 38 markets and still growing. Our Global Expansion Team takes SumUp&#39;s payment products into new countries, with Mexico and Canada among our most recent launches and more markets like New Zealand and Argentina on the way. As a QA Engineer in our Berlin payments team, you&#39;ll build the automated and manual tests that decide when a new card reader can go live in a market, across frontend, backend and mobile flows, and you&#39;ll also help complete L3 certification (the final round of testing that acquiring banks and card networks require). It&#39;s hands-on engineering work with real launch impact, because your tests help new markets go live and recently launched ones stay stable, so small businesses there can take card payments with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain frontend and backend test automation, with mobile where relevant, and add targeted regression tests to continuous integration (CI) workflows so market specific checks run consistently after code changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test SumUp products across markets, with a mix of automated and manual testing, functional, integration and regression checks, plus edge cases and recovery scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot ways to improve how we test, explain why they matter and make a convincing case for the changes with the biggest payoff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trace failures through complex payment flows using logs and transaction traces, then raise clear, prioritised defects and work with engineers and external partners until they&#39;re fixed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the testing of end-to-end communication between a payment terminal, software applications, and an acquiring network. with acquiring banks and card networks, and keep the team informed on certification status, quality risks and release readiness so launch decisions rest on evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely in collaboration with engineers, product and market-launch teams, as well as acquirers, card schemes and certification labs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming or scripting skill to build and maintain automated tests for frontend web and backend APIs, and comfort reading code in languages such as Golang, Kotlin, Java or others on our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/en-us/how-we-work/the-sumup-tech-radar/&quot;&gt;Tech Radar.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing software both manually and with automation, including turning requirements into test scenarios and deciding what to automate first based on customer, launch and technical risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyse logs, transaction traces and test results, and to write defect reports that include reproduction steps, expected versus actual behaviour, impact and evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with Git and Jira (or similar tools)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL and test-data setup, contract testing, mocking or service virtualisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engineering mindset: the ability to spot what can be improved, explain the reasoning and persuade others with clear evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A curious, ownership minded approach: seeking out context when things are unclear and using AI tools where they help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Card payments, payment terminals, acquirers, card schemes or certification labs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market launches, device integrations, external technical partners or business-to-business communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Payments experience is helpful but not required. We&#39;ll support you in learning card payments, devices and the certification process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide, from our Berlin office. This involves an office-first set up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💶 A corporate pension scheme where we match up to 20% of your contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏖️ Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave plus public holidays and special leave days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚵🏾‍♂️ Numerous other benefits such as Urban Sports Club subsidy, Kita placement assistance, subsidised office lunches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team builds, tests, deploys, and monitors the classifiers that block internal agents from taking dangerous actions. These classifiers run across RL, evals, and internal deployments, and are designed to catch things like sandbox escape attempts or exfiltration of sensitive data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When a classifier flags an action, it can &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/news/improving-alignment-security-efforts&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;block the action before the tool call runs, end the task, and alert a human&lt;/a&gt;. This is one layer of a defence-in-depth with several layers that reinforce each other: what our classifiers flag feeds into offline monitoring, and the findings from that go back into better classifiers and safer environment design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work combines research and production engineering:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The research problem is building high recall and high precision classifiers to catch rare, novel, and sometimes adversarial behaviour. There are also several narrow research questions to answer - for example, how to deploy safety classifiers inside training environments without incentivising models to evade them. Some research also builds on the multi-stage designs described in our work on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/claude-code-auto-mode&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Claude Code auto mode&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/research/next-generation-constitutional-classifiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Constitutional Classifiers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The engineering problem is shipping these classifiers into the critical path of research and product work. These classifiers need to cover a huge volume of traffic while operating within cost, latency and availability constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, much of our work is done with Claude: you&#39;ll direct agents to run experiments and ship code, and review what they produce. That moves the hard part of the job towards deciding what to do and in what order. Additionally, organisation, communication, and prioritisation skills matter a great deal as our classifiers sit in the path of many other teams&#39; work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design, train, and evaluate classifiers that detect unsafe agent actions in real time, owning pieces such as prompted models, trained classifiers, or probes on model internals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deploy, tune and operate these classifiers in the critical path of internal agents, RL training, and evaluations, and own their accuracy, reliability, latency, cost, and failure behaviour&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the datasets, labelling pipelines, and evaluations that allow us to measure and improve our classifiers and harm taxonomies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with red teaming colleagues to stress-test our classifiers, and harden them against what they find&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with the teams whose agents, environments, and evaluations we run on, so that false positives get fixed quickly without weakening protection&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to the team&#39;s direction, including what to build, what to partner on, and where to invest&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to organise and prioritise several parallel streams of work, and to communicate clearly with the teams that work affects&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to critically review code and experiment results, including work produced by AI agents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sincere interest in developing safe and beneficial AI systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading ambiguous technical projects and setting direction for other engineers or researchers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience evaluating large language models, developing classifiers, or operating high-scale production systems where requirements change quickly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience building detection systems where true positives are rare and false positives are costly, such as abuse, fraud, spam, or intrusion detection&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience running low-latency, high-availability services that other systems depend on, including being on call for them&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience fine-tuning language models, or working with probes and other methods that read model internals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with LLM inference or serving infrastructure, or with integrating new components into training infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background in security, such as sandboxing or detection and response&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with research on AI control, scalable oversight, agent safety, or reinforcement learning&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£375,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£640,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For roles performing work in California: &lt;/strong&gt;We will consider for employment all qualified applicants, including those with arrest or conviction records or criminal histories, in a manner consistent with the requirements of applicable state and local laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the City of Los Angeles’ Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you ----- addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job__description body&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;The Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;Grafana Labs is looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Account Executive, Growth&lt;/strong&gt; based in Germany who will be responsible for prospecting and closing new business across DACH. You will identify, nurture and close opportunities with new customers, manage forecasts and track customer data. We&#39;re strong proponents of a consultative sales approach - learn about the customer&#39;s needs first before talking products. Your expertise will be critical in helping articulate the value of our products, work with the customer during the trial phase and hand off a strong relationship to our Growth team. Ideally, you come from a technical background and have sold technical products before.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet and exceed individual quarterly and annual sales goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outbound prospecting into net-new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage all aspects of the sales process (prospecting, sales meetings, product demos, proofs of concept, proposals, and negotiations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate sales through outbound prospecting and inbound leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be able to understand and convey the value of both Grafana Cloud and Grafana Enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert in managing your sales pipeline in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage quote creation, order processing, and day-to-day customer requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ Years of experience in infrastructure technology sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of consistent goal achievement in a highly competitive environment (top 10% performer)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Energetic, upbeat, entrepreneurial, tenacious team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable and with demonstrable experience in high velocity technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will need to be an excellent communicator in all channels (in person, online, in writing) and able to form strong working relationships both in person and virtually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English &amp;amp; German&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bonus Points For:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with open source technology is a significant advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Command of the Message and MEDD(P)ICC is ideal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Rewards&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Germany, the OTE compensation range for this role is EUR 175,000 - EUR 185,000&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt; Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;*Compensation ranges are country specific. If you are applying for this role from a different location than listed above, your recruiter will discuss your specific market’s defined pay range &amp;amp; benefits at the beginning of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Thrive at Grafana Labs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;100% Remote, Global Culture -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;As a remote-only company, we bring together talent from around the world, united by a culture of collaboration and shared purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling Organization&lt;/strong&gt; – Tackle meaningful work in a high-growth, ever-evolving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transparent Communication&lt;/strong&gt; – Expect open decision-making and regular company-wide updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation-Driven&lt;/strong&gt; – Autonomy and support to ship great work and try new things.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Source Roots&lt;/strong&gt; – Built on community-driven values that shape how we work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empowered Teams&lt;/strong&gt; – High trust, low ego culture that values outcomes over optics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career Growth Pathways&lt;/strong&gt; – Defined opportunities to grow and develop your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Approachable Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; – Transparent execs who are involved, visible, and human.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Passionate People&lt;/strong&gt; – Join a team of smart, supportive folks who care deeply about what they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Person onboarding &lt;/strong&gt;- We want you to thrive from day 1 with your fellow new ‘Grafanistas’ to learn all about what we do and how we do it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Balance is Key&lt;/strong&gt; - We operate a global annual leave policy of 30 days per annum. 3 days of your annual leave entitlement are reserved for Grafana Shutdown Days to allow the team to really disconnect. &lt;em&gt;*We will comply with local legislation where applicable.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Grafana Labs is an equal opportunities employer. We welcome applications from everyone regardless of race, colour, nationality, origin, caste, sex, gender reassignment identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, religion or belief, disability, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, maternity, marital, family or carer status, or any other characteristic which is protected by local law. We believe that equality and diversity build a strong organisation, and we work hard to ensure that is the foundation of our organisation as we grow.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Grafana Labs may utilize AI tools in its recruitment process to assist in matching information provided in CVs to job postings. The recruitment team will continue to review inbound CVs manually to identify alignment with current openings.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;For information about how your personal data is used once you’ve applied to a job, check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://grafana.com/legal/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
